pdf_create_signature_widget() reports a failure instead of returning a
deleted widget.

When filling in the new widget threw (e.g. the form's /Fields isn't an array),
the catch deleted the widget from the page and then returned it as if it had
worked, keeping the caller's reference: our Sign PDF went on to sign a widget
no longer on the page. Now it drops the reference and rethrows.
(Idea from Vira Reader's mupdf-signature-errors.patch.)

diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-form.c b/source/pdf/pdf-form.c
index 4f0a2fd18..acae86e91 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-form.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-form.c
@@ -1087,8 +1087,16 @@ pdf_create_signature_widget(fz_context *ctx, pdf_page *page, char *name)
 	}
 	fz_catch(ctx)
 	{
+		/* SumatraPDF: report the error; the widget is deleted, so it mustn't
+		 * be returned (the caller would sign a widget no longer on the page) */
 		pdf_abandon_operation(ctx, page->doc);
-		pdf_delete_annot(ctx, page, annot);
+		fz_try(ctx)
+			pdf_delete_annot(ctx, page, annot);
+		fz_always(ctx)
+			pdf_drop_annot(ctx, annot);
+		fz_catch(ctx)
+			fz_rethrow(ctx);
+		fz_rethrow(ctx);
 	}
 	return (pdf_annot *)annot;
 }
